# Design docs: HTML layering + principle diagrams

**This rule is always on.** Applies whenever the agent writes or substantially revises a **technical design** (living `docs/superpowers/specs/` `§`, new/edited plan that locks architecture, or a `docs/superpowers/` as-built architecture explainer).

## Must deliver (same change)

1. **Core layering** — which trees/namespaces own which lane (e.g. UI / CPU prep / GPU submit).
2. **Principle diagram** — data/control flow for the locked architecture (stages, barriers, thread ownership).
3. **HTML artifact** — self-contained `.html` (inline CSS; optional CSS/JS animation for staged pipelines). Prefer Chinese UI labels; keep code paths / API names in English.

Markdown may keep a short ASCII sketch, but the **HTML is normative for visuals**. Link it from the `§` / plan metadata (`Diagram:` line).

## Placement

| Doc kind | HTML path |
| --- | --- |
| Living `§` / open plan / as-built explainer | `docs/superpowers/diagrams/<topic>.html` (one topic → one file; revise in place) |

Do **not** invent a parallel diagram tree under `src/`. Do **not** rely on Mermaid-only or external image hosts as the sole visual.

## Visual style (locked): light technical

Use a **light architecture / docs** palette — print-friendly, high contrast, calm. Do **not** copy the dark shell style of `docs/superpowers/diagrams/views-window-process.html` for new design diagrams.

| Token | Guidance |
| --- | --- |
| Page bg | Near-white / cool gray (`#f4f6f8`–`#fafbfc`) |
| Panels | White cards, 1px cool gray border (`#d8dee6`) |
| Text | Near-black (`#1a2330`); muted secondary (`#5a6a7e`) |
| Accent | Single calm blue for links / active stage (`#2563a8`) |
| Lane colors | Soft tinted fills + darker label text (UI / schedule / CPU / GPU) — not neon on black |
| Code | Slightly darker than body on light gray chip |

Avoid: dark mode default, purple glow, heavy multi-shadow, marketing gradient hero.

## HTML bar

- Copyright header + `<!DOCTYPE html>`; **light technical** CSS per table above.
- Show **layers** (stack or swimlanes) and **principle flow** (arrows / numbered stages).
- Pipelines with time/order (FrameJob, prep×N, present): add a **simple animation** that clarifies “who waits / who never joins”.
- No network CDN (inline CSS/JS only).

## Don’t

- Don’t ship architecture-only Markdown with no linked HTML diagram.
- Don’t default new design diagrams to dark theme.
- Don’t duplicate a second dated design file just to hold the HTML — colocate under `docs/superpowers/diagrams/`.
- Don’t skip the diagram when “only appending a §” if that `§` locks a new architecture or parallel model.

